r/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269779} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1c3ef1-3087-5ea3-b5b1-7a4019e7e484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269975} {:answer/id #uuid "763f82a2-56c6-5a1f-bae5-b2e830e0d2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270314} {:answer/id #uuid "91f46875-57d2-5226-a483-28c9319b00a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270543} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9381c5-58eb-5004-ac29-e32be74e7faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d9381c5-58eb-5004-ac29-e32be74e7faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270665} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d52c12-5ef6-542e-afe9-0934d4bb8136" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19d19949-a1e1-5f2c-a86b-bf0e96de0dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-141286" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272259 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12210f84-5313-563f-a57f-e1153ca41c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Converges to $\\frac{7}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269428} {:answer/id #uuid "325153df-9203-538e-8a85-7c97347b3b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Converges to $-\\frac{7}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269726} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7ac92a-e6b9-5306-b6bf-8470d5f8d1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Converges to $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270082} {:answer/id #uuid "99194c28-bf4f-58a2-99e3-8086ab7a7a4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Converges to $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270615} {:answer/id #uuid "d67977f3-0395-57a9-aca8-bf042270bdd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d67977f3-0395-57a9-aca8-bf042270bdd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271149} :answer-field/id #uuid "964be632-4152-563d-8164-08d2b1d6baf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28e36c28-53cf-5ecc-9bb5-73b0ad09588f" :question/math-academy-id "q-141312" :question/problem "Does the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{4{(-7)}^{n}}{{2}^{n}}$ for $n\\ge 1$ converge or diverge? If it converges, what is its limit?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{4{(-7)}^{n}}{{2}^{n}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{(-7)}^{n}}{{2}^{n}} \\\\  & =4{(-\\frac{7}{2})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now see that this is the geometric sequence with $r=-\\frac{7}{2}.$ \n\nSince $|r|>1,$ the sequence diverges."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272260 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30847f0b-0b4b-5f36-a3b0-37f3dad54553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Converges to $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269706} {:answer/id #uuid "545f1118-43f6-5a00-8098-f3be2988683a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Converges to $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270021} {:answer/id #uuid "578fba5d-47fa-5591-9315-034b97234804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270042} {:answer/id #uuid "78b7a0e1-7f04-5430-9f17-d26da04c9f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Converges to $\\frac{11}{9}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270339} {:answer/id #uuid "edad3d6a-2c87-516e-bac4-fb514407d70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Converges to $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "578fba5d-47fa-5591-9315-034b97234804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270042} :answer-field/id #uuid "f78976ba-707b-5d42-8224-1405db058378" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "385046ae-9549-5d03-b987-27cdd162ac0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-141314" :question/problem "Does the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{8\\cdot {11}^{n}}{{9}^{n}}$ for $n\\ge 1$ converge or diverge? If it converges, what is its limit?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{8\\cdot {11}^{n}}{{9}^{n}} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{{11}^{n}}{{9}^{n}} \\\\  & =8{(\\frac{11}{9})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now see that this is the geometric sequence with $r=\\frac{11}{9}.$ \n\nSince $|r|>1,$ the sequence diverges."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e082063-0bec-52c0-9abb-ccfd65629060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269835} {:answer/id #uuid "73fdf72c-3fcc-55d7-b59a-2a42f091f341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270293} {:answer/id #uuid "97e6d079-ff4a-5073-8f18-1ff573cc25fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270606} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd06048-2d47-53ef-85a1-abd7a31133d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271349} {:answer/id #uuid "ff1b5d28-56a1-52d2-aca2-940b6a405673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff1b5d28-56a1-52d2-aca2-940b6a405673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271499} :answer-field/id #uuid "89bbb705-bc82-52a8-990a-0598294a9982" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cba8d40e-9ff0-576c-b4c2-5a73d8552590" :question/math-academy-id "q-141322" :question/problem "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=8{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThis given sequence is a geometric sequence with common ratio $r=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}.$ Since ${x}^{2}$ is positive, $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges if \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,0<{x}^{2}\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTaking into account the fact that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\n0<x\\le 2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145b8ac2-e119-5bb5-97b4-57b7f6c36df8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269448} {:answer/id #uuid "23b49514-142c-5ec7-b618-4ff74f034103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269582} {:answer/id #uuid "83d2c3b6-5dd1-5ee8-9fca-f3e5a69a70d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270407} {:answer/id #uuid "c10a13ae-f2e1-5b81-ac68-d491a279c9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270980} {:answer/id #uuid "cfef26a9-ce94-5d52-8b32-42f376028599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "145b8ac2-e119-5bb5-97b4-57b7f6c36df8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269448} :answer-field/id #uuid "be528d01-eb38-5742-aef2-18fc25b51ab4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "342f5e64-a399-5f8b-a691-0fd529d174f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-141323" :question/problem "Consider the geometric sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{x}{4}{(\\frac{8}{x})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{8}{x}.$ \nSince $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{8}{x}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,x\\ge 8.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0064e8e7-084c-5f2c-84fe-7c01c9b6b635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269261} {:answer/id #uuid "327cce87-0e05-561c-a911-f266e9362209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269731} {:answer/id #uuid "5728834c-7cf8-5195-8511-c4b4832275ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270037} {:answer/id #uuid "94939561-af80-514a-a98b-f8ec53c93c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270569} {:answer/id #uuid "d13ae2d7-1ace-5094-a5f0-dc31fa47ace3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0064e8e7-084c-5f2c-84fe-7c01c9b6b635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269261} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe4db61b-63d8-5a32-b074-5e668b6c2a1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c6a32232-02fb-5219-8889-a984024d7a02" :question/math-academy-id "q-141329" :question/problem "Consider the geometric sequence ${a}_{n}=2x{(\\frac{16}{{x}^{4}})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{16}{{x}^{4}}.$ \nSince ${x}^{4}$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{16}{{x}^{4}}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{4}\\ge 16.\n$$\n\nTaking into account the fact that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\nx\\ge 2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c76b1f7-d307-5022-b523-2a9d701df0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269821} {:answer/id #uuid "458f17d5-ae3c-5206-88da-0f8f9e8c40ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269904} {:answer/id #uuid "95ddf996-8bf3-5861-ba6b-942a4fee4bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270585} {:answer/id #uuid "b185b23a-d4dd-5aaa-ab15-5d137417fe8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270856} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b0195a-a623-51e6-b397-aa476e1870d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c76b1f7-d307-5022-b523-2a9d701df0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269821} :answer-field/id #uuid "9037fd3f-bf8c-5555-9427-c1f893b2831d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df355f69-884b-5a24-91f1-5877dbb36e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-141332" :question/problem "Consider the geometric sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{x}{2}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.$ \nSince ${x}^{2}$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}\\ge 2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTaking into account the fact that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\nx\\ge \\sqrt{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "207ab9ff-69d5-5e9e-a049-8b6583bc05af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269542} {:answer/id #uuid "2f98f3e6-62fd-5c6d-92e4-50c671d9ca0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269693} {:answer/id #uuid "3b1ea3bb-790a-5ccb-8e4e-128a05b493ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269807} {:answer/id #uuid "43bc6e1e-cd04-50cd-be5f-4fc3762ad2df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269880} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c6a97b-676e-5ce3-a1dd-2814966863b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43bc6e1e-cd04-50cd-be5f-4fc3762ad2df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269880} :answer-field/id #uuid "8034b0e3-22f2-5777-8701-11ede3b31369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b45c8d5b-a164-5f47-b24d-aad447830fc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-141336" :question/problem "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{2n}}{{16}^{n+1}},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{x}^{2n}}{{16}^{n+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2n}}{16\\cdot {16}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2n}}{{16}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}.$ Since ${x}^{2}$ is positive, $r$ is also positive.  So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for\n\n$$\n0<\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,0<{x}^{2}\\le 16.\n$$\n\nTaking into account that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\n0<x\\le 4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272268 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6211bc13-073a-5c99-9605-93ab7fbe77de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270130} {:answer/id #uuid "62e2123a-428e-5278-bf29-291ac8d69565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{84}{85}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270142} {:answer/id #uuid "8fb5a56e-15bc-5b67-a314-22d25895a411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270523} {:answer/id #uuid "da82b6f7-cbf7-5284-96b2-ed3d8e44c5e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271182} {:answer/id #uuid "e1452372-7a2e-52a8-8a7f-a4b98a03c469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{36}{85}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1452372-7a2e-52a8-8a7f-a4b98a03c469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{36}{85}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271247} :answer-field/id #uuid "cccef8e9-e6b1-5778-a676-5f08c8b73531" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa20e82e-b00e-53d9-aae3-c53c2db1c9a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-141357" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{8}{17},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{4}{5},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v).$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{8}{17})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{8}^{2}}{{17}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{64}{289} \\\\  & =\\frac{289}{289}-\\frac{64}{289} \\\\  & =\\frac{225}{289}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{225}{289}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{15}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{15}{17}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{17})(\\frac{3}{5})-(\\frac{15}{17})(\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{85}-\\frac{60}{85} \\\\  & =-\\frac{36}{85}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70772ebb-922a-557a-9ea9-f54d6d437fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270264} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e2ba4e-1030-54b7-bb9e-52eeaa51ec52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270732} {:answer/id #uuid "afb75370-3708-5e38-be35-0de44709eb35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270834} {:answer/id #uuid "d4bc3b99-7b00-52dd-a05c-66df48bef76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271139} {:answer/id #uuid "f22eb4a3-842c-506f-9e15-5e501d2c0cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70772ebb-922a-557a-9ea9-f54d6d437fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270264} :answer-field/id #uuid "f03ebea0-4a7a-5a11-a858-d951b06424b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f15816e-a4ea-5e54-ac29-0fac8d7bc4b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-141360" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{12}).$\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-\\frac{\\pi }{12}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aff4cbe-6fe4-5b7e-818d-a180abe9eb18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269488} {:answer/id #uuid "1ebb1f5f-41ff-5401-ad84-cc41307a79d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269527} {:answer/id #uuid "38362095-3b1c-5bfd-9cc4-30473fe3b5bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269776} {:answer/id #uuid "4003a8ec-c9e7-5741-ba8f-90325c814912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269851} {:answer/id #uuid "ea19c52e-9497-565a-b200-4435179ca96d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4003a8ec-c9e7-5741-ba8f-90325c814912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269851} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcc5eb38-7a7e-586b-9f31-c5ca7c948e10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c98a2195-4ec8-5e2a-a4f5-76fb1079c255" :question/math-academy-id "q-141374" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{150}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v={150}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{150}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{150}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b931fa1-ee52-5db3-bac9-497efc06f498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269370} {:answer/id #uuid "2342b124-c9e0-58c0-a580-8d4f8695808a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269577} {:answer/id #uuid "69b15b7b-0cac-5374-93f1-818c8990768a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270207} {:answer/id #uuid "a358caaa-5c57-5746-b54c-5548bfb79b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270725} {:answer/id #uuid "dff6ea96-0ee2-5bc4-80b8-7b9f1617a512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b931fa1-ee52-5db3-bac9-497efc06f498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269370} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f2bd73b-78d1-5e9e-92ad-582b63f4ea0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "308956a9-f5f0-59d1-8748-67ba18adb1f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-141381" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49fb6310-1708-5e9d-87d7-81b3f3f0f7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269939} {:answer/id #uuid "7094b20c-23f3-5650-858b-219773020164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270266} {:answer/id #uuid "9258bad9-66f5-57da-a3a7-c822fae4b159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270548} {:answer/id #u