er-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a22d57d-9107-5ef5-9e1a-664d1e481595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269651} {:answer/id #uuid "2e7bf421-a5a6-51a7-bbde-dcaec6ed4724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269688} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0c5476-651b-5c29-aaf7-9c8b4495a59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270462} {:answer/id #uuid "8a8eb468-d843-5e6f-a576-53b1846a95f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270466} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8ff2c0-77a5-54e0-af66-4eb8ca206ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a22d57d-9107-5ef5-9e1a-664d1e481595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269651} :answer-field/id #uuid "64d9c7cb-8c90-5531-a052-3b459d3163b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bedf2d85-2b35-59e9-bfbf-70576d25817c" :question/math-academy-id "q-141386" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall  the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272281 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70a4198d-a723-5135-9077-d2f5ff0021ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270267} {:answer/id #uuid "77d4d412-0b0e-5644-b9b3-cdac878109ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270332} {:answer/id #uuid "a4bfa82f-86f4-52b0-842e-d8de0b71d9b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270740} {:answer/id #uuid "b044cd5a-47a8-5254-b3cb-e1312d62f4dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270840} {:answer/id #uuid "c7982b78-f76c-556e-9dbe-4f6e74e17244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4bfa82f-86f4-52b0-842e-d8de0b71d9b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270740} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d498f1c-7e55-59d7-a359-5d2d6958f785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c51674c-fd7a-5949-82f4-633efacaa379" :question/math-academy-id "q-141444" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{6}-b\\sqrt{3}}{15},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{4}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{16}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{25}-\\frac{16}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})(-\\frac{3}{5})+(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3})(\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{15}+\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}-3\\sqrt{3}}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=4,b=3,$ and $a+b=7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272293 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38ed7dc5-6698-544e-8bd2-b698be8286f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269786} {:answer/id #uuid "3e36f179-7a99-5b80-b4d9-f5843fe8a371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269838} {:answer/id #uuid "775b0e34-1455-5f81-80d8-cdd1da12224b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270325} {:answer/id #uuid "a28998c9-f966-53ff-9806-5302008f6b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270718} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c01206-6b1c-516a-bfe3-0aaf6c038975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a28998c9-f966-53ff-9806-5302008f6b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270718} :answer-field/id #uuid "18991195-bded-5020-8432-b563eaa7724a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54091288-1b32-5047-b279-479983ae80b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-141522" :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}+x-2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x-2\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}$, writing the constant term $-2$ last:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31012e79-2696-578b-952b-a385f9bb0eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269711} {:answer/id #uuid "80e62b24-0b58-586c-ab5e-10a92a99e5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270386} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8982a4-a551-5a56-96cc-144410267cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270506} {:answer/id #uuid "94a242c2-81bc-53a1-99fc-de5cfa4e26aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{11}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270571} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa96b06-cbed-595d-86c7-fdb048fe292f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{11}{4})}^{2}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31012e79-2696-578b-952b-a385f9bb0eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb